params.body:
Verkennen and Netwerk show what Bouwsoft knows. What a successor needs on top of that lived only in a relation's tag note in Netwerk. That note covered relations and nothing else, and it held one text per relation. This makes every node that opens a place to add context for the handover, and gathers it all on one page.

## Context on every node

A panel "Context voor de overdracht" appears wherever a node opens:

| Where | Node | Anchor |
|---|---|---|
| Verkennen, an opened project | project | `project:<Bouwsoft key>`, or `site:<id>` for a project only the app knows |
| Verkennen, an opened person | person | `person:<key>` |
| Verkennen, an opened machine or material | machine, material | `machine:<name>`, `material:<name>` |
| Netwerk, a selected relation | relation | `relation:<Bouwsoft key>` |

A project uses its Bouwsoft key, the same key Netwerk uses for projects. So when Netwerk projects get a panel, they will show the same notes.

Each note has:
- **a kind:** what the successor must know, a habit or agreement, a risk, or who takes it over;
- **the text;**
- **who knows it today:** the same three carriers as the relation tags, optional;
- **who takes it over:** optional;
- **who wrote it and when.**

A node holds as many notes as people tell. A note can be deleted after a confirm. The office and a shared link may both add notes, as with tags. Relation tags themselves do not change.

## Overdracht

`/overdracht` is a new item in the menu, also for a shared link. It shows:
- every note grouped by node, each node one click from where it opens;
- counts per kind, which filter the list;
- a "Wie weet het vandaag" bar, which filters by carrier;
- filters on node type and words;
- a CSV with the same filters.

The notes on relation tags from Netwerk are included as "Wat de opvolger moet weten", so nothing told earlier is left out.

## Design

`context_notes` is one row per statement: anchor, type, a label kept as written, kind, text, carrier, successor, author. This is the hand-entered part of the knowledge graph in `docs/graphs.md` (on `workbench/graph-design`): anchored on the network keys, each row a statement with its author and moment. When the full model (`kg_nodes`, `kg_evidence`) comes, these rows become evidence with provenance `tapped`, each on the node its anchor names.

## Tests

`HandoverTest` covers:
- a note is kept with kind, carrier, successor and author, validated, and can be deleted;
- an unknown anchor type is refused;
- a project's note shows in Verkennen and on Overdracht with a link back;
- Overdracht gathers notes and relation tag notes, and filters on carrier, kind and type;
- the CSV follows the filters;
- a relation's note shows in Netwerk;
- a shared link may add a note under its own name, and strangers are sent to the login.

Full suite 238/238, JS 13/13, pint clean. Walked through in headless Chromium on a copy of the production-size database: add context on a project in Verkennen and on a relation in Netwerk, then see both on Overdracht. The page loads in 34 ms, with no horizontal scroll at 390 px.

After merge: `php artisan migrate` (one new table).

